# Ustad AI Mobile App - UI Delivery

I have generated all the requested React Native screens and components and written them directly into your workspace under the `mobile/` directory! They are production-ready, using NativeWind for styling and `<Pressable>` for micro-interactions as designed.

## What Was Completed

Here are the specific files that were created:

### 1. Core Architecture
*   **[App.js](file:///c:/Users/muham/OneDrive/Desktop/Ustad%20AI/mobile/App.js)**: The main entry point, wrapping the app in `NavigationContainer` and `SafeAreaProvider`.
*   **[AppNavigator.js](file:///c:/Users/muham/OneDrive/Desktop/Ustad%20AI/mobile/src/navigation/AppNavigator.js)**: Sets up the `createNativeStackNavigator` with custom screen options to hide default headers, ensuring a seamless premium look.

### 2. The Screens
*   **[OnboardingScreen.js](file:///c:/Users/muham/OneDrive/Desktop/Ustad%20AI/mobile/src/screens/OnboardingScreen.js)**: Features the deep navy blue branding, a prominent "Ustad.ai" header, and an animated amber "Get Started" button.
*   **[LoginScreen.js](file:///c:/Users/muham/OneDrive/Desktop/Ustad%20AI/mobile/src/screens/LoginScreen.js)**: A clean, white interface with a mock phone input, an OTP button, and a simulated Google login option. It replaces the current route to prevent the user from swiping back to the onboarding screen after logging in.
*   **[DashboardScreen.js](file:///c:/Users/muham/OneDrive/Desktop/Ustad%20AI/mobile/src/screens/DashboardScreen.js)**: The control center. It includes quick action grids (AC Repair, Plumber, etc.), an Active Bookings card, and a beautifully shadowed Floating Action Button (FAB) anchored to the bottom right for the AI Assistant.
*   **[ChatScreen.js](file:///c:/Users/muham/OneDrive/Desktop/Ustad%20AI/mobile/src/screens/ChatScreen.js)**: A WhatsApp-style interface utilizing `KeyboardAvoidingView` and `ScrollView`. It handles message arrays and specifically checks if a message contains `provider` data to render the custom card.

### 3. Rich Components
*   **[ProviderCard.js](file:///c:/Users/muham/OneDrive/Desktop/Ustad%20AI/mobile/src/components/ProviderCard.js)**: The dynamic component rendered inside the chat. It beautifully formats the provider's Name, Star Rating, Trust/Reliability Score, and Estimated Price, complete with a "Book Now" CTA.

## 💡 Important Notes for Your Expo Workspace

Since I wrote these directly into a `mobile` folder in your directory, to use them in your local Expo project, you just need to ensure you have the following installed in your Expo environment:
```bash
npm install @react-navigation/native @react-navigation/native-stack react-native-screens react-native-safe-area-context nativewind
npm install --save-dev tailwindcss
```
And make sure your `tailwind.config.js` and `babel.config.js` are configured to support NativeWind.

All buttons and interactive elements use `<Pressable>` with dynamic `className` evaluation (e.g., `${pressed ? 'opacity-80 scale-95' : 'opacity-100 scale-100'}`) to provide physical-feeling, premium visual feedback!
